/-!
# The original six-space in the actual constrained moved section

Literal component placement puts the original orbit, which is generated by
its residual commutators, in [starV,K]. Its natural-plus-dual action has no
fixed vector, so the original orbit remains injective after quotienting the
moved section by its full fixed space. This embedding is fixed by the actual
radical image. Both the moved module and its central quotient have dimension
at least six.

The full B.5.1 conclusion is retained. Dimension excludes natural SL4/SL5
and one-copy repeated natural rows. The orthogonal six-space and its
seven-dimensional cover, exterior dimension ten, natural-plus-dual, and
repeated natural rows with at least two copies remain explicit.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith C.4.5--8 and 12.1.11, pp.152--154,794.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory Representation Representation.BinaryOffender
open scoped MatrixGroups IsMulCommutative
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter12.Section02.ChosenModule
open Chapter4 Chapter4.Section04 Chapter4.Section02.RankOneReciprocalEscape
